  "interpretation": "Diagnostic measurement, not a gate and not an ARC or biological-advantage result. Two findings bear on the declared configuration. First, sensory drive needs three anatomical hops and four internal steps to move all 1,314 descending neurons, so the declared K=2 leaves the readout blind on the first decision and lagged thereafter. Second, cross-action memory has a half-life of two actions in both conditions, which is set by the leak term rather than by recurrence through the graph. The real and weak-null graphs differ sharply in pathway depth, readout magnitude, and readout dimensionality, but barely in cross-action memory. The weak null preserves in-degree and per-row weight multisets only; it is not the preregistered directed degree-preserving null and no real-versus-null claim may rest on it.",
